{"commit_sha":"20bd591e58100d3d5b64a61fb8e65ca1abb77ae7","position":"1793827323163342001-292bbc78-6742-4dc3-8738-4ff20204fed3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"8129482698d3f1e7f97324274314ee8417cacfae506067837b2a0f1318332a7a","event_uuid":"7e5e7f8d-d065-4f0c-816c-3c8af98ef74a","position":{"commit_sha":"0349a36c1a3ba8d430660ae0fe8ca0df294fe5a1","position":"1793827838736611001-7e5e7f8d-d065-4f0c-816c-3c8af98ef74a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"7c55ea12c0312f09d52871101cc9d31daf7b5a3c7dc4d0ef9d760a7930f060f0","event_uuid":"4d2b69ec-6bb8-4e32-b38f-73e9ad840d89","position":{"commit_sha":"01e0d6c2e716638ea33bdb9cd4c15811c130e5bf","position":"1793828345070765001-4d2b69ec-6bb8-4e32-b38f-73e9ad840d89"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"23d29c1193620aae5bf8078026b4513b88dfe32e513b75cee09714297daffd24","event_uuid":"5cc4e070-8458-4d8d-b3f2-54226e322372","position":{"commit_sha":"4e1ab33d4bb44fb4f61ba9278a8bd4c91dd346b2","position":"1793828348634684001-5cc4e070-8458-4d8d-b3f2-54226e322372"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision: a run whose only unsuccessful jobs never got a runner casts the existing no-label 'cancelled' vote-type (Verified stays 0 after clear-vote; the CANCELLED message and triage comment still post). Precedent: d1d4-8c8b-e2c5-4ac2 (commit b45ce2a490a) made cancelled runs comment-only no-vote outcomes; this reuses that path. ADR 0114 governs adding/promoting required gates and is not engaged: no job enters or leaves the Verified aggregate, and the new snapshot step is continue-on-error input to normalize. Root cause: inside the reusable build-and-test workflow a not-acquired matrix cell does not surface as a 'cancelled' needs result, so FAILURE_OBSERVED=false and the normalize CONCLUSION expression fell through to fail-closed 'failure' (all 4 runs logged CONCLUSION=failure FAILURE_OBSERVED=false -> vote-type=failure). Discriminator (jobs API): runner_id 0, runner_name empty, steps []. Survey of the last 200 Gerrit Verified Gate runs: 19 cancelled jobs matched it, 26 cancelled-after-start jobs all had a runner and 25-29 steps. Auto re-queue rejected: needs actions: write in the job holding the Gerrit vote key. Fail-closed: any other failed/cancelled-with-steps job, FAILURE_OBSERVED=true, or a missing/invalid snapshot keeps Verified -1.","timestamp":1793812279825385001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit change 3311 patch set 1 merged at LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (run 41897584396) with 0 unresolved comments, submitted revision-scoped via scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py. Merged SHA on main and the GitHub mirror: 4c4e9b2f0ba89663c9d6ac86c7297690288d6106. Deploy: the Gerrit Verified Gate workflow is dispatched on main and its vote job sparse-checks out scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py from the dispatched ref on a GitHub-hosted runner, so merge plus mirror sync is the deploy; no production-host component changed. Tests: new module tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py went from 6/19 passing on main to 19/19; 196 targeted tests pass after rebase; make lint and make typecheck exit 0. make verify: 20788 passed, 2 failed in tests/interfaces/facades from a cross-test logging leak unrelated to this change (filed fibre-beamy-angora, discovered_from); that directory passes 815/815 in isolation. LLM-Review advisories: a queued job cancelled for another reason also matches (no tests ran, so no verdict is accurate); the in-progress vote-job exclusion is pinned by name to the workflow, and a mismatch falls back to failure, never to a false +1.","timestamp":1793822278853198001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close refused (no force used): the 3311 workflow step's '# mechanism-ok:' marker named this ticket as its sunset ticket, and src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py refuses to close a ticket whose marker is still in the tree. Follow-up change 3321 removes the mechanism rather than repointing it: the jobs fetch moves into the existing, baselined normalize step (fetched only when the aggregate is failure with nothing observed failed; a failed fetch keeps the fail-closed failure). Mechanism census 647 -> 646 active, make lint exit 0, make typecheck clean, 1544 related tests pass. New tests run the step's own shell with a stub gh: failed fetch -> failure, captured not-acquired payload -> cancelled, success -> no fetch.","timestamp":1793825212971659001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793809356101891001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2b8a24d0-97ed-48bd-8f89-b91c7c4e7359","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fe33-81e0-b027-42e8"},{"link_uuid":"5b5cf274-64bc-4a28-a878-391016ebc549","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6b7d-ee19-45b7-439d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn 2026-11-04 PST, 4 Gerrit Verified Gate runs (41855161578, 41856506741, 41857357120, 41857377497) cast Verified -1 although every job that ran passed. In each run the only unsuccessful job was `build-and-test / pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)`, cancelled with the annotation \"The job was not acquired by Runner of type hosted even after multiple attempts\" plus a macOS arm64 capacity notice. Each change then needed a manual `recheck`. Authors and agents read -1 as a verdict on their change when none exists.\n\n## Root cause (observed)\n- The vote job's normalize step logged `WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION: cancelled` (im-open aggregate), `CONCLUSION: failure`, `FAILURE_OBSERVED: false` -> `vote-type='failure'` in all 4 runs.\n- `FAILURE_OBSERVED` false means no `needs.*.result` was `failure` or `cancelled`, so the `contains(needs.*.result, 'cancelled') && 'cancelled'` branch (`.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, normalize step `CONCLUSION`) never fired. The reusable `build-and-test` caller result was also not `success`, so the full-route completeness check failed and the expression fell through to its fail-closed `'failure'`.\n- So the no-verdict path added for superseded runs (ticket d1d4-8c8b-e2c5-4ac2, commit b45ce2a490a: \"cancelled -> comment-only no vote\", `scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py` `_VOTE_TYPES[\"cancelled\"]` casts no label) is unreachable when one matrix cell inside a reusable workflow is cancelled.\n- The jobs API distinguishes the cases. Across the 45 cancelled jobs in the last 200 runs, all 19 never-acquired jobs had `runner_id: 0`, `runner_name: \"\"`, `steps: []`; all 26 cancelled-after-start jobs had a runner id and 25-29 steps. No job mixed the two.\n\n## Approach\nFollow the d1d4 precedent: a run whose only unsuccessful jobs were never given a runner carries no test verdict, so it gets the existing `cancelled` vote-type (no label, the existing `CANCELLED: <run url>` message and triage comment; Verified stays 0 after clear-vote). This reuses the existing no-vote path instead of adding a new outcome. Automatic re-queue was not chosen: it needs `actions: write` in a workflow that holds the Gerrit vote key, and d1d4 already fixes the non-verdict semantics.\n\n1. `scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py` (stays one stdlib-only file; `tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port.py::test_entry_point_is_stdlib_only`): add `runner_never_acquired(job)` (conclusion `cancelled`, no steps, no runner id, no runner name) and an optional jobs input read from the file named by `JOBS_FILE`. `normalize()` returns `cancelled` instead of `failure` only when ALL of these hold: conclusion is exactly `failure`, `FAILURE_OBSERVED` is not `true`, the jobs list loads, at least 1 job is a never-acquired cancellation, and every other job except the in-progress vote job (`cast Verified`) concluded `success`, `skipped` or `neutral`. Any missing/unreadable/invalid jobs file, any failed job, or any cancellation with steps or a runner keeps `failure` (fail closed). Existing two-input behaviour is unchanged when `JOBS_FILE` is unset.\n2. `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` vote job: inside the existing normalize step, best-effort fetch this run's jobs (only when the aggregate is failure and nothing observed failed) (`gh api --paginate repos/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID/jobs`, already permitted by `actions: read`) into the `JOBS_FILE` path under `$RUNNER_TEMP` that normalize reads; a failed fetch leaves no file. No separate workflow step and no new mechanism. The script still comes from the trusted default-branch sparse checkout.\n\n## Scope\n- scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py\n- .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml\n- tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py (new)\n- tests/fixtures/ci_jobs/ (new: captured jobs-API payloads)\n- tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py (workflow wiring assertions)\n- tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py (find the normalize step by id; the new snapshot step shifts its index)\n\n## Testing\nFixtures are captured jobs-API payloads, read-only: run 41855161578 (not-acquired macOS job 126662869315), job 126547335283 from run 41821258615 (cancelled after 29 steps with a runner), and job 126249875159 from run 41731188733 (macOS `failure`, Module-size gate step failed). The mid-test and genuine-failure runs are built by substituting those captured jobs for the macOS job in the 41855161578 job set. Write the tests first and confirm they fail on current main.\n- not-acquired run + `failure` -> `cancelled`\n- mid-test cancellation -> `failure`\n- genuine macOS failure -> `failure`\n- not-acquired plus any other failure -> `failure`; `FAILURE_OBSERVED=true` -> `failure`\n- missing / empty / invalid `JOBS_FILE` -> `failure`; `JOBS_FILE` unset keeps the existing table\n- workflow: the jobs snapshot step precedes normalize, is `continue-on-error`, and normalize receives `JOBS_FILE`\nNo autouse fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A job cancelled because no runner was acquired (no steps executed) does not produce Verified -1 as if tests failed; the chosen behaviour (automatic re-queue of that job, a distinct non-verdict outcome, or another mechanism consistent with ADR 0114 on gating CI) is decided and recorded on this ticket. Checked by the not-acquired fixture test returning `cancelled` and a ticket comment recording the decision and its d1d4 precedent.\n- [x] A test reproduces the classification from a captured jobs-API payload for a not-acquired cancellation and for a genuine cancellation mid-test, and asserts they are treated differently. Checked by `pytest tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py` passing (and failing on main before the fix).\n- [x] A genuine macOS test failure still produces Verified -1. Checked by the captured macOS-failure fixture test returning `failure`.\n- [x] `make lint` (incl. actionlint, zizmor, mechanism and complexity ratchets) and `make typecheck` exit 0, and `pytest tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion.py tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port.py tests/scripts/test_cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` passes.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The fix merges to main through Gerrit at LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; the merged SHA is recorded in a ticket comment. The vote job sparse-checks out these scripts from the default branch, so merging is the deploy.\n  provenance: environment=production Gerrit rebar.solutions.navateam.com and the navapbc/rebar GitHub mirror; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — change 3311 read over the Gerrit REST API at status MERGED with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, and the merged SHA 4c4e9b2f0ba89663c9d6ac86c7297690288d6106 fetched from origin/main; follow-up change 3321 read at MERGED with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, merged SHA 3c9d6efd69413584ae5ff90285f1fe35be176d17 fetched from origin/main.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py","reason":"classify never-acquired-runner cancellations as the no-vote cancelled outcome"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"snapshot run jobs before normalize and pass JOBS_FILE"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_unacquired.py","reason":"fixture-driven classification tests"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/ci_jobs/","reason":"captured jobs-API payloads"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py","reason":"workflow wiring assertions"},{"path":"t